PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A. Clockwise direction, origin near ton

The phrasing "prolonged expression of the azis gene before others" indicates an early time-of-entry for azi (i.e., azi lies immediately proximal to the origin of transfer) together with a relatively large physical gap to the next selected marker in the direction of transfer. On the standard E. coli linkage map the azi locus lies immediately adjacent to ton. Therefore an Hfr origin placed near ton, with F integrated so that chromosomal transfer proceeds clockwise (thr-leu-azi-ton-…), places azi first among the markers being scored and creates the observed temporal separation before subsequent markers enter. The other listed origins (lac, pro, thr, str) are all more distant from azi and would not produce an early, isolated azi entry time.}

}

