PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A. Clockwise direction, origin near ton

The E. coli chromosome is mapped with standard markers in the order thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac-gal-str (circular, ~100 min total). Hfr strains initiate linear transfer from the F integration site (origin) in a fixed direction (clockwise or counterclockwise) that depends on F orientation. “Prolonged expression of azis before others” indicates azi enters the recipient substantially earlier than subsequent markers, which occurs only when the origin lies immediately adjacent to azi with transfer proceeding away from the azi-ton cluster. Option A places the origin next to ton (adjacent to azi) and orients transfer so azi is the first marker mobilized, producing the observed temporal gap before the next genes appear. The other options either start far from azi or send transfer in the opposite direction, so azi would not appear first or alone for an extended interval.}

}

