3.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Standard E. coli order (min increasing): thr(0)–leu–azi–ton–pro–lac–gal–str(73+). “Prolonged azi expression before others” = azi is proximal/earliest marker (large temporal gap to next scored marker), requiring origin immediately upstream of azi with transfer oriented toward/through azi.  
Colleagues split: majority favor A (clockwise near ton) assuming that polarity sends azi first; Col10 favors D (counterclockwise near thr) for same reason; Col5/9 favor B (near lac, CCW).  
Key unresolved: exact clockwise vs. CCW convention in this problem (HfrH classically sends thr-leu-azi-ton first, matching either clockwise-from-thr or CCW-from-ton depending on map drawing). No option lists “clockwise near thr”; thus D or A may be intended once polarity label is fixed. No figure given, so map order + early-entry logic is the only evidence. Will track which colleagues revise polarity claim next round.}

