9.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Standard marker order thr–leu–azi–ton–pro–lac–…–str remains undisputed. “Prolonged azi expression before others” requires azi to be the single most proximal marker after oriT, creating a long gap to every subsequent scored marker. This geometry is achieved only by an origin adjacent to the azi–ton cluster with transfer oriented into azi first (i.e., the reverse of the thr→azi direction).  
Majority (2,3,4,6,8,9,11) continue to select A, citing adjacency of ton and claiming “clockwise” polarity mobilizes azi first; several of these responses contain internal contradictions on what “clockwise” actually means relative to minute numbering. Minority positions: 10 reiterates D (thr-origin, counterclockwise) on the grounds that only that pair places azi immediately distal; 1,5,12,7 now converge on B (lac-origin, counterclockwise) because it sends transfer lac→pro→ton→azi, making azi early among tested markers.  
Persistent unresolved issue: direction label vs. map convention (minutes increase clockwise, so ton→azi is counterclockwise). No new map figure supplied; polarity terminology remains the main source of disagreement. My updated assessment: logical geometry favors an origin near ton with the polarity that drives transfer into azi; whether the question’s label “clockwise” matches that polarity is still unclear, so A remains the plurality choice but D or B are defensible if the label is inverted. No consensus shift yet.}

